# mouse: packets as a Microsoft mouse sends them (the key script's {mouse},
# handed to the driver as IRQ4 would): moves right and down, left with the
# left button, far down against the screen's edge, then both buttons, which
# end the command.
program: shell
keys: {wait 20}mouse\n{wait 5}{mouse 16 8 -}{wait 2}{mouse -40 0 L}{wait 2}{mouse 127 127 -}{wait 2}{mouse 0 0 LR}
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>mouse
Move the mouse; Esc or both buttons end.
x 320, y 100 (column 40, row 12), buttons: none
x 336, y 108 (column 42, row 13), buttons: none
x 296, y 108 (column 37, row 13), buttons: left
x 423, y 199 (column 52, row 24), buttons: none
x 423, y 199 (column 52, row 24), buttons: both
A:\>
